@host = http://localhost:3000
@adminEmail = admin.seguridad@example.com
@adminPassword = AdminSecure123

### D0. Preparación: registrar admin de pruebas
# @name register_admin_security
POST {{host}}/api/user/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### D0.1 Validar email admin (poner code real de BBDD)
PUT {{host}}/api/user/validation
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{register_admin_security.response.body.token}}

{
  "code": "718462"
}

### D0.2 Login admin
# @name login_admin_security
POST {{host}}/api/user/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### D1. Error por no enviar token
GET {{host}}/api/user

### D2. Login con password incorrecta (debería 401)
POST {{host}}/api/user/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "PasswordIncorrecta999"
}

### D3. Crear company inválida (isFreelance false sin campos requeridos)
PATCH {{host}}/api/user/company
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login_admin_security.response.body.token}}

{
  "isFreelance": false
}

### D4. Cambio de contraseña inválido (newPassword igual a currentPassword)
PUT {{host}}/api/user/password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login_admin_security.response.body.token}}

{
  "currentPassword": "{{adminPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### D5. Refresh token inválido
POST {{host}}/api/user/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "token.invalido"
}

### D6. Invite sin rol admin o sin company (debería 403/4XX)
# Ejecuta este request con un token de usuario guest si quieres validar autorización por rol.
POST {{host}}/api/user/invite
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login_admin_security.response.body.token}}

{
  "email": "error.invite@example.com",
  "password": "InviteError123",
  "name": "Error",
  "lastName": "Invite",
  "nif": "33333333P"
}
